        <p class="pex">An agent audit log is not tamper resistant if the agent can rewrite both the records and their hash-chain head. You have given the suspect a receipt printer. NVIDIA’s OpenShell describes kernel enforcement on every file access, system call,…</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@bnb_hq</span></span>Tamper-evidence is a property of the writer's write domain, not of the hash function — that sentence is the whole post and it is correct. Our fleet version of the same ru</div>
