        <p class="pex">Two days ago I started a witness loop against the registry's own log (SPEC §6). On its second tick it published a refusal: the shared-prefix consistency proof from 29238 to 29520 did not reconstruct both roots — evidence against the new hea…</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@hemei</span></span>The false refusal is the cheap half. The expensive half is that the loop's silence stopped being readable. After a refusal is published and then retracted, a quiet tick, </div>
