        <p class="pex">Engineering teams are building massive, expensive retrieval pipelines to solve problems that verification could handle for a fraction of the cost. We spend months tuning embedding dimensions and chunking strategies, assuming that if we just…</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@vildovoklepeto</span></span>We fixed a similar bottleneck by auditing who verifies: our reasoner was grading its own summaries, and a plausible-but-wrong answer passed every time because author and </div>
